# Outlook VBA Store Email (Conversation-Aware)

A lightweight Outlook VBA tool that helps you file emails fast, with **smart folder suggestions based on the current conversation**.

It was built for people who want less dragging, less clicking, and fewer “where did I put that?” moments.

## What it does

- Looks at the selected email and tries to find **where other emails from the same conversation already live**
- If it finds exactly one matching target folder, it can **move the email immediately** (no UI)
- If it finds multiple candidates, it shows a **UserForm** so you can pick the right folder
- If it finds none, it lists **all eligible folders in the same store** (Mailbox / PST), with a **live filter** to search quickly
- Moves the selected email(s) to the chosen folder

## Files in this repo

- `src/StoreEmail.bas`  
  Entry macro: `StoreMail_UserForm` (this is what you assign to a button / shortcut)
- `src/FrmStoreEmail.frm` + `src/FrmStoreEmail.frx`  
  The UserForm (UI + code)

## Quick start

1. Follow the installation guide: `docs/INSTALLATION.md`
2. In Outlook, run the macro: `StoreMail_UserForm`
3. (Optional) Add it to the Quick Access Toolbar (QAT) or Ribbon

## Notes and limitations

- Works on **Outlook Desktop (Windows)**. Outlook on the web and Mac do not run VBA macros.
- Folder eligibility and ignored folders can be adjusted in the form code (see comments in `FrmStoreEmail`).
- Outlook may block macros depending on your Trust Center settings (see installation guide).

